issues.issue:
C3's rule ('≥3 of 4 pairs locally faster, 8 seeds, log-rank p<0.05; otherwise narrow the paper') is underpowered and treats absence of evidence as evidence of absence.

Simulation at between-seed log-sd 0.25:
- per-pair power at n=8: 0.46 at ratio 1.3, 0.26 at 1.2;
- P(≥3 of 4 pairs significant): 0.24 when every pair is truly 1.3; 0.06 at 1.2; 0.01 when two pairs are 1.3 and two are null;
- a pooled stratified log-rank on the same 32 runs per arm: 0.97, 0.74 and 0.44.

Per-pair 80% power needs about 16–18 seeds per arm at 1.3 and about 32 at 1.2.

