recommendations:
PR-3 Arms.
Primary arms:
- M: frozen + probe-region floor;
- G: frozen + global floor, tuned for global;
- F: ft + critic warm-up + KL limit + tuned global floor;
- K: kickstart with tuned anneal + floor;
- R: frozen + random-region floor, a fresh draw per seed, coverage-matched;
- P: frozen + source-success-predicate region.
Secondary arms, 1 expert × 4 seeds, descriptive with Holm: plain ft, plain kickstart, scratch+floor (γ tuned), LP-FT, PEX, residual RL, novelty×competence, anti-seam, lab floor 0.6.

PR-6 Primary hypotheses, tested in a fixed sequence at α=0.05 two-sided; stop at the first non-rejection:
- H1: M vs F;
- H2: M vs K;
- H3: M vs G (each at its tuned dose);
- H4: M vs R (location at matched coverage);
- H5: M non-inferior to P (upper 95% bound of the time ratio below 1.2).
Test: log-rank stratified by pair × expert. Effect sizes: a pooled AFT log-normal time ratio with a 95% CI from a cluster bootstrap (experts within pairs, seeds within experts), plus per-pair RMST(τ) differences and per pair × expert time ratios.

PR-10 Secondary endpoints, Holm within the family:
- T50 and T90;
- AUC over [0, H];
- final success at H (mean of the last 3 evaluations);
- stability: maximum drawdown within 2M after T80, and the fraction of post-T80 evaluations ≥0.7;
- fraction reaching 0.8 by τ (Kaplan–Meier with CI);
- dispersion: IQR of log T80.
Report wall-clock only from a dedicated one-job-per-GPU benchmark. Follow Agarwal et al. 2021: interval estimates and performance profiles, never bare means or medians.

PR-11 Mechanism, as pre-specified plots without tests:
- T_ignite vs T_learn;
- per-iteration realised std inside and outside the region, region occupancy, open-while-grasped events, drops;
- yield-check dose–response and overlap–dose curves per expert, with Wilson CIs, including an equal-open-command-budget comparison;
- a 128-env stress replicate of M vs G.

PR-13 C4 gate, offline, before any multi-task RL:
- concentration per hidden layer, excluding the readout;
- task-label permutation over whole episodes as the null;
- split-half Spearman ≥0.5;
- ranking on a validation split;
- 20 random-unit draws and 3 seeds;
