feasibility.verdict:
The plan is not feasible as written.
- Two of its five claims cannot be built and run by Jan 15 on two shared 4090s: C4 (multi-task RL with six structural or gradient baselines) and C5 (vision/VLA).
- The RSS assumption is wrong: the only RSS 2027 entry point is a 6-page extended abstract due Dec 4, 2026, and concurrent submission is forbidden.
- The C3 rule will most likely reject a real effect of about 25%.

It becomes feasible, with roughly a week of slack before Nov 22 and the holidays as a buffer, if cut to:
- C1–C3 plus the C2 locality controls, two non-extension controls and an offline C4 diagnostic;
- Stack, PlaceCube or PlaceSphere, and PushRetreat, with 3 source experts per pair;
- baselines: LP-FT, residual, novelty x competence, fine-tuning plus floor and kickstart plus floor;
- realised-noise logging and a matched-mean global arm;
- a pre-registered pooled stratified analysis;
- the venue decided at the Nov 22 gate.
